<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  Task 3 Coordinated Logistics, the USV's half. handbook 3.3.4.

  ONE TREE FOR ALL THREE TIERS. Core stops once the fire is out; Advanced and
  Disruptive go on to read the resource request off the same window.
  TierAtLeast is what tells them apart, from the goal's tier.

  WHAT THE COURSE DOES, and why the tree is this shape:

    three bays, numbered LEFT TO RIGHT FACING THEM. Each has a RED or GREEN
    docking indicator at the base of its face; exactly one is GREEN.
    Dock in the GREEN one and report DockingReport(bay_id).
    THEN, and only then, one of that bay's two windows lights RED. Spray it
    until it turns GREEN (5 s), report FirefightingReport(window_id).
    Disruptive: off 1 s, then c1 1 s / off 1 s / c2 1 s / off 2 s, for 60 s.
    c1 is the tin, c2 the circle. Report ResourceDeliveryRequest and relay it
    to the UAV.

  THE NUMBERS BELOW COME FROM TWO PLACES, and change when either does:

    the dock   RobotX 2026 build guide ("Docking Bay Structure"): 0.5 m dock
               cubes; three 1.5 m slips between 0.5 m fingers 2.0 m long, so
               the bays are 2.0 m apart; each face a 1 m square at the back of
               its slip, on the main deck.
    the boat   ~1.0 m long, 0.6 m wide; camera 0.37 m ahead of the body origin
               and 0.41 m above the water (Resources.md).

  1. BAYS ARE KNOWN BY WHERE THEY ARE. DockObservation's bay_index is "left to
     right in THIS frame", so a boat that sees two bays is told 0 and 1
     whichever two they are. The runner places every sighting in the world and
     folds it into a track (dock::DockBook); the bay NUMBER comes from sorting
     three confirmed tracks along the dock (dock::layout).

  2. LOOK FROM WHERE ALL THREE FIT, AND NEVER FROM INSIDE A SLIP. 5 m out, the
     outer faces sit ~22 deg off the bow - well inside the camera's ~39 - and
     the indicators are inside the 6 m the CV reads them reliably at. The
     fingers end 2 m out, so 5 m clears them with the whole hull. Further looks
     are head on to whichever bay has the fewest readings, from the same 5 m.
     If nothing is seen from the approach point at all, a ring search looks
     out from it in five directions before giving up.

     No strafing. It exists in MANUAL on this hull, but a tree driving MANUAL
     means RC overrides from the companion, which are G1-gated (README safety
     rule 3) - and nothing here needs it. Every look is reached via a lead point
     further out, because the camera faces forward and GuidedSetpoint.yaw is
     discarded: the heading a boat stops with is the direction it arrived from.

  3. STRICT, THEN LENIENT. SafeBayKnown(need_others_red) wants GREEN + RED +
     RED, the consistent picture. Only after every look has been spent does the
     lenient form accept a lone strong GREEN with the others unread.

  4. THE CHOICE CAN BE UNDONE ON THE WAY IN. ChosenBaySafe re-reads the
     committed bay's RECENT indicator readings on every tick of the berthing
     legs. A run of REDs halts the leg and the retry starts the search again -
     where those recent reds now veto that bay.

  5. ENTER STRAIGHT, FROM OUTSIDE. Lead-in (5 m), line-up (3 m) and berth
     (1.25 m) sit on the bay's own centreline, measured face to body origin.
     The line-up point is outside the fingers - 2.0 m of finger, half a hull,
     margin - so the boat is straight before its bow is between them. The
     berth leaves the stern inside the fingers (1.25 + 0.5 + along_tol <= 2.0)
     and the bow clear of the face. LinedUp skips the lead-in when the boat is
     already there (it is, whenever the survey ended head on to this bay).

     PRECONDITION: WP_RADIUS well under the berth tolerance (0.25 m); 0.2 m is
     what the sim runs. ArduRover calls a GUIDED destination reached inside
     WP_RADIUS and loiters where it stopped; this boat's is 2.0 m, which parks
     it at the finger ends and leaves the enter leg waiting for an arrival that
     never comes. tools/task3_sim reproduces it (test_e2e wp_radius_2).

     KNOWN LIMIT, NOT FIXED HERE: once berthed, GUIDED holds by loitering
     (LOIT_RADIUS 2.0 m) and cannot strafe, and the slip leaves 0.45 m either
     side. A 5 cm/s cross-current puts the hull on a finger in ~10 s.

  6. THE FIRE. AwaitFireTarget re-sends the docking report until RoboCommand
     confirms it (a lost report is a fire that never lights). SprayUntilHit aims
     every tick at the CV's aim point and switches the cannon OFF on every exit.

     THE CAMERA MUST SEE THE UPPER WINDOW FROM THE BERTH, and level it cannot:
     berthed, it is ~0.9 m from the face and 0.41 m up, and the upper window's
     top is ~1.2 m up - 41 deg above level, against the ~19 deg the camera sees
     above its axis once the CV's 188-row hull band is masked. It needs ~20 deg
     of pitch-up (cam_pitch_deg ~ -20) or a higher mount. With it level, a fire
     in the upper window is never seen and AwaitFireTarget times out. The sim
     models this (test_e2e upper_window_level / upper_window_pitched).

  THE GUARD BAND is re-ticked every tick and halts everything below it.
  DockCameraAlive is in it because the dock detector publishes every frame,
  bays or not: silence means the node is dead, and a blind boat must not keep
  driving at a dock. UpdateDockBook never fails (see task3_leaves.cpp).

  TIMEOUT AND CANCEL live in the runner, not here.
  UNDOCKING is not here: leaving the slip needs a stern-first move, and the
  setpoint path is position-only. The boat holds in the berth when this ends.
-->
<root BTCPP_format="4" main_tree_to_execute="CoordinatedLogistics">
  <BehaviorTree ID="CoordinatedLogistics">
    <ReactiveSequence name="guard_band">

      <IsAutonomous/>
      <DockCameraAlive max_age_s="3.0"/>
      <UpdateDockBook/>

      <Sequence name="task3">

        <SetTask token="TASK_COORDINATED_LOGISTICS"/>

        <!-- Find the bay, commit, line up - all OUTSIDE the slips. A failure
             anywhere in here (the chosen bay turning RED on the way in, say)
             starts the search again with everything learned so far. -->
        <RetryUntilSuccessful num_attempts="3" name="dock_attempts">
          <Sequence name="find_and_dock">

            <ReactiveFallback name="find_safe_bay">
              <SafeBayKnown need_others_red="true"/>
              <RetryUntilSuccessful num_attempts="4" name="looks">
                <Sequence name="look">
                  <PickVantage standoff="5.0" lead_m="2.0" out="{vantage}" lead="{lead}"/>
                  <!-- Via the lead: the last leg is driven AT the dock, so the
                       boat stops facing it. -->
                  <NavigateTo target="port" goal="{lead}" tolerance="1.0"/>
                  <NavigateTo target="port" goal="{vantage}" tolerance="1.0"/>
                  <!-- WATCH, then call the look a failure so the retry moves on.
                       Readings accumulate the whole time; SafeBayKnown above
                       ends this the moment they settle it.

                       NOT HoldStation: that re-sends the CURRENT position while
                       the boat is still moving, so it overshoots the new point
                       and turns round to go back to it - away from the dock it
                       is meant to be watching. The vantage setpoint stands; the
                       autopilot stops there and loiters, facing in. -->
                  <ForceFailure>
                    <Sleep msec="12000"/>
                  </ForceFailure>
                </Sequence>
              </RetryUntilSuccessful>
              <SafeBayKnown need_others_red="false"/>
            </ReactiveFallback>

            <CommitSafeBay/>

            <!-- Onto the centreline from OUTSIDE the line-up point, so the
                 boat reaches it already heading in. Skipped when it is already
                 there - a lead-in behind the boat would turn it round twice. -->
            <Fallback name="lead_in">
              <LinedUp min_along_m="2.7" lateral_tol="0.4" heading_tol_deg="20.0"/>
              <ReactiveSequence name="to_lead">
                <ChosenBaySafe min_ema="0.3"/>
                <DockWaypoint point="lead" predock_m="3.0" berth_m="1.25" lead_m="2.0" out="{goal}"/>
                <NavigateTo target="port" goal="{goal}" tolerance="1.0"/>
              </ReactiveSequence>
            </Fallback>
            <ReactiveSequence name="line_up">
              <ChosenBaySafe min_ema="0.3"/>
              <DockWaypoint point="predock" predock_m="3.0" berth_m="1.25" lead_m="2.0" out="{goal}"/>
              <NavigateTo target="port" goal="{goal}" tolerance="0.4" resend_m="0.2"/>
            </ReactiveSequence>

          </Sequence>
        </RetryUntilSuccessful>

        <!-- IN THE SLIP FROM HERE ON, AND OUTSIDE THE RETRY ON PURPOSE. A retry
             starts with a lead-in point 5 m out - BEHIND a boat that is in a
             slip - and GUIDED reaches a point behind by turning round, which
             in a 1.5 m slip means hitting the fingers. There is no reverse on
             the setpoint path. So a failure past this point fails the mission,
             loudly, for the operator to recover by hand. -->

        <!-- berth_m is face to BODY ORIGIN: the bow is 0.5 m ahead of it, so
             1.25 leaves ~0.75 m off the face and the stern ~0.25 m inside the
             finger ends. -->
        <ReactiveSequence name="enter">
          <ChosenBaySafe min_ema="0.3"/>
          <DockWaypoint point="berth" predock_m="3.0" berth_m="1.25" lead_m="2.0" out="{goal}"/>
          <NavigateTo target="port" goal="{goal}" tolerance="0.25" resend_m="0.2"/>
        </ReactiveSequence>

        <!-- WAIT UNTIL DOCKED, up to 10 s: the boat arrives inside tolerance
             still settling, and one sample taken mid-swing is not the answer.
             Inverter / KeepRunningUntilFailure / Inverter is BT for "run until
             this condition holds". DockedInBay tests the whole HULL against
             the slip the boat measured, not just its middle. -->
        <Timeout msec="10000">
          <Inverter>
            <KeepRunningUntilFailure>
              <Inverter>
                <DockedInBay along_tol="0.25" lateral_tol="0.3" heading_tol_deg="15.0"
                             hull_length="1.0" hull_beam="0.6" finger_margin="0.35"/>
              </Inverter>
            </KeepRunningUntilFailure>
          </Inverter>
        </Timeout>

        <ReportDocking/>

        <AwaitFireTarget timeout_s="60.0" resend_s="10.0"/>
        <SprayUntilHit timeout_s="60.0" min_green_s="0.4" max_aim_age_s="1.0"/>
        <ReportFirefighting window_id_base="1"/>

        <!-- Core ends here. Above it, the same window carries the request. -->
        <Fallback name="request">
          <Inverter>
            <TierAtLeast tier="1"/>
          </Inverter>
          <Sequence name="read_and_report">
            <DecodeResourceRequest timeout_s="80.0" hold_s="5.0" min_frames="20"/>
            <ReportResourceRequest/>
          </Sequence>
        </Fallback>

      </Sequence>
    </ReactiveSequence>
  </BehaviorTree>
</root>
